@@ -158,3 +160,22 @@ Andrews RJ, Rouse WB, O'Leary CA, Booher NJ, Moss WN. (2023). ScanFold 2.0: a ra
 ## Support
 
 For issues or questions, please open an issue on GitHub
+
+## secondrna multi-FASTA compatibility
+
+The upstream parser already accepts multiple FASTA records. These modifications
+prevent per-record output overwrites. FASTA IDs (the first whitespace-delimited
+header field) must be unique and must not contain path separators. Duplicate or
+unsafe IDs and empty input are rejected before outputs are created.
+
+For multiple records, `structure_basename` is `{basename}.{record_name}`; for a
+single record it remains `{basename}`. CT/DBN filenames retain their historical
+single-record form. ALL-pairs files now use `{structure_basename}.ALL.bp` (this
+also changes the older concatenated single-record BP filename). Guides use
+`{structure_basename}.README.md`. Multi-record IGV sessions use
+`{structure_basename}.igv_session.json`; single-record sessions retain
+`igv_session.json`. Scan CSV, FinalPartners, filtered BP and WIG filenames remain
+record-specific and unchanged. The shared run log records source SHA-256 hashes.
+
+The secondrna repository distributes the full patch and upstream revision under
+`vendor/scanfold2/`, with installation and regression-test instructions.
